  "summary": "dnspython has excessive memory and CPU use",
  "details": "### Summary\n\nA maliciously crafted zone file could use a WKS record to consume excessive memory and CPU, possibly causing the process to exit due to memory exhaustion.\n\n### Details\n\nThe `from_text()` parser does not check that a WKS record service number is between 0 and 65535 inclusive.  It then uses this number to resize the bitmap to accommodate a bit with that offset.  This can cause extremely large memory allocations, and also extends the array very inefficiently, wasting CPU.\n\n### Proof of concept\n\nThis demonstrates the failure to limit the service number, though with a value that does not cause excessive memory or CPU consumption.\n\n```\nrd = dns.rdata.from_text(\"IN\", \"WKS\", \"10.0.0.1 udp 65536\")\n```\n\n### Impact\n\nIf dnspython is used to read zonefile format where the attacker can control the type and rdata text, the program may consume excessive memory or CPU, denying service.",
